And there are people who make no claim. 

"I believe god exists", is, as far as I can see, _not_ a claim 
about the existence of gods, but about the existence of a belief.

Similarly "I do not believe in gods" and "I believe there are no 
gods" are not claims other than about a belief position.

"god exists"
"gods do not exist"
"the existence of gods is unknown/unknowable"
are, on the other hand, claims about the true state of affairs.

The first trio of claims (about belief), seem to me to be related 
to atheism and theism, whereas the latter 3 are about knowledge, or 
its lack (agnosticism).


 
